{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1515","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1515","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1515\",\"parent_revision\":\"13da5ca6dfcaa5efccb9c5ba73a63e562e2b6b6509ccf1714f69dafbe9d46366\",\"root_revision\":\"13da5ca6dfcaa5efccb9c5ba73a63e562e2b6b6509ccf1714f69dafbe9d46366\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe feature-verifier quality gate (T2 in complete-implementation) runs pytest and static analysis but never exercises the actual MCP server dispatch path. Changes to MCP server code can pass all tests and type checks while the live wiring is broken \u2014 because tests import the code directly, bypassing FastMCP&#39;s routing layer entirely. This leaves deployments validated on paper but unobserved in the path that actually runs in production. `fastmcp call --command` can exercise the full dispatch path against source files without requiring a session restart or cache rebuild, but it is not currently part of any quality gate.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"The feature-verifier quality gate (T2 in complete-implementation) runs pytest and static analysis\\\" \u2014 Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 443-452 confirm T2 maps to the `feature-verifier` agent. The agent file (`plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md`) confirms Steps 3-6 run CLI/file checks and grep-based structural verification.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"never exercises the actual MCP server dispatch path\\\" \u2014 Evidence: `feature-verifier.md` Step 8 (Live Delivery Surface Validation, lines 249-341) is conditionally driven by `quality_gates.live_validation` in `.dh/language-manifest.yaml`. When absent, it emits `LIVE_VALIDATION: SKIPPED` and continues \u2014 no fastmcp smoke test is executed by default and none is hardcoded for MCP projects.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"`fastmcp call --command` can exercise the full dispatch path against source files\\\" \u2014 Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` lines 355-406 document the exact pattern using `--command \\\"uv run python $(pwd)/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py\\\"`. This exercises the full FastMCP routing layer without a session restart.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"no fastmcp call smoke test executed against run_sam_server.py\\\" for P912 \u2014 Evidence: Session observation is consistent with the gap: Step 8 only fires when `live_validation` is declared in the language manifest. If no manifest entry exists for a project, the step silently passes.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: `missing-guardrail`\\n\\nRoot cause: Step 8 of `feature-verifier` delegates live validation to a project-managed `.dh/language-manifest.yaml` field (`quality_gates.live_validation`). For MCP server projects that do not declare this field (or where the manifest does not exist), the live dispatch path is never exercised. There is no fallback smoke test for projects detected as containing MCP servers.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md:249-341` \u2014 Step 8 Live Delivery Surface Validation (modify: add MCP server detection branch before manifest check)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md:355-406` \u2014 Reference `fastmcp call --command` pattern for SAM and backlog servers (read-only reference for exact command syntax)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py:1-33` \u2014 SAM server runner (target of smoke test)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` \u2014 Backlog server runner (secondary target)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nfastmcp CLI call syntax (from `CLAUDE.md` lines 367-395):\\n\\n```bash\\n# SAM server smoke test\\nuv run fastmcp call \\\\\\n  --command \\\"uv run python $(pwd)/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py\\\" \\\\\\n  --target sam_list \\\\\\n  --input-json '{}'\\n\\n# Backlog server smoke test\\nuv run fastmcp call \\\\\\n  --command \\\"uv run python $(pwd)/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\" \\\\\\n  --target backlog_list \\\\\\n  --input-json '{}'\\n```\\n\\n`--command` is required (not optional) because the server files use relative imports that break when run directly. SOURCE: `CLAUDE.md` lines 393-395.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMCP server code changes that break FastMCP routing (wrong tool names, missing `@mcp.tool()` decorators, import path errors in runner scripts) pass all quality gates and receive `status:verified` while the live dispatch path is silently broken. Observed: P912 marked verified with this gap.\\n\\nSeverity: High \u2014 silent failure, no indication to developer that the MCP wiring was never exercised.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.dh/language-manifest.yaml` for the development-harness project should be created or updated as part of this fix so that the `live_validation` field is the canonical record \u2014 this prevents the smoke test from being re-derived heuristically on every run\\n- No other issues block this fix\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `feature-verifier` Step 8 detects when the project contains an MCP server runner script (presence of `scripts/run_*_server.py` or `mcp:` block in any `plugin.json`) and executes a `fastmcp call` smoke test against it, regardless of whether `live_validation` is declared in the language manifest\\n- [ ] Smoke test command uses the exact pattern documented in `CLAUDE.md`: `uv run fastmcp call --command \\\"uv run python $(pwd)/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py\\\" --target {tool_name} --input-json '{}'` \u2014 substituting the actual runner script path and a known lightweight tool (e.g., `sam_list` for SAM server, `backlog_list` for backlog server)\\n- [ ] When the smoke test exits non-zero or produces a traceback in stderr, `feature-verifier` records `LIVE_VALIDATION: FAIL` and returns `STATUS: GAPS_FOUND` \u2014 not `VERIFIED`\\n- [ ] When no MCP server runner is detected and `live_validation` is absent, the existing `SKIPPED` path is preserved (no regression)\\n- [ ] The gap between \\\"no manifest\\\" and \\\"no smoke test\\\" is documented in `feature-verifier.md` Step 8 with an explicit MCP detection branch in the flowchart\\n- [ ] A `.dh/language-manifest.yaml` entry for `quality_gates.live_validation` in the development-harness plugin is added as the canonical reference for MCP smoke tests, pointing at `run_sam_server.py` and `run_backlog_server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: S\\nReasoning: Change is confined to `feature-verifier.md` Step 8 \u2014 add a MCP server detection branch (glob for `run_*_server.py`, check `plugin.json` for `mcp:`) then run the fastmcp call command and evaluate exit code. The command syntax is already documented in `CLAUDE.md`. No Python code changes required \u2014 this is a skill/agent documentation change that the orchestrator reads and executes.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **feature-verifier quality gate missing live mcp smoke test** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-04-05: P912 marked status:verified with no fastmcp call smoke test executed against run_sam_server.py\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c8f6ce9228c5808cd576d41b7bd43b1d666528b7c458e790325fb9ce05e1f806\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdryaA\"}"}